# `cargo fuzz init` generates this file with `corpus` in it. That line is
# deliberately absent here: the seed corpora under `corpus/` are checked
# in, because a fuzz target with no seeds starts from a single empty
# input and spends its first minutes rediscovering that source code has
# braces in it. Every crasher we find is also committed here, so the
# artifact survives independently of anyone re-running the fuzzer.
#
# Everything below is build output or a run's scratch space. `Cargo.lock`
# is *not* here: it is tracked, like `enums/Cargo.lock`, because the
# `make fuzz-check` clippy pass runs `--locked` and Dependabot needs a
# lockfile to raise a PR against.
target
artifacts
coverage
# Where libFuzzer writes the inputs it discovers. `make fuzz-smoke` /
# `fuzz-run` hand it this directory first and `corpus/` second, so the
# committed seeds stay read-only and a run never dirties the tree.
corpus-work
